<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  ForgottenArsenal.xml      Jawa_Patches · authored 2026-08-14
  ============================================================================

  Builds FACTION_SPEC.md section 13: the Forgotten Arsenal, a label-only reskin
  of vanilla `Mechanoid`.

  🔴 THE UNBOUND HIVE WAS CUT FROM THIS FILE, 2026-08-14. It reskinned vanilla
  `Insect`, and `Insect` is on an UNTICK row of
  `infrastructure/state/WORLDGEN_FACTION_CHECKLIST.md` section 2 — the owner
  turns it off at the world screen, so a label patch on it can never be seen.
  DECIDE cut the faction; the roster went 14 -> 13. `Mechanoid` is on no untick
  row, so this half is unaffected.
  ⇒ Before reskinning ANY vanilla faction, confirm its vessel is absent from
  that checklist's untick sections. This is the second thing that list has
  caught.

  READ FROM THE SHIPPED DEF, 2026-08-14 ; not inferred:
  C:\Program Files (x86)\Steam\steamapps\common\RimWorld\Data\Core\Defs\
    FactionDefs\Factions_Hidden.xml

      Mechanoid   ParentName FactionBase · label "mechanoid hive" ·
                  hidden true · permanentEnemy true · techLevel Ultra ·
                  factionNameMaker NamerFactionMechanoid ·
                  6 Combat pawnGroupMakers · NO settlementGenerationWeight node

  It carries `label` and `description` on the def itself, so both are `Replace`,
  never `Add`.

  🔴 LABEL AND DESCRIPTION ONLY, ON PURPOSE.
  `hidden true` is CORRECT and stays: the Forgotten Arsenal is a what, not a
  who. It has no leader, no settlements and no diplomacy, and it never needed a
  `settlementGenerationWeight` node because it has none to begin with.

  ⛔ It inherits its `pawnGroupMakers` wholesale. Alpha Mechs and several other
  mods patch `Mechanoid`'s group makers directly, and every mechanoid raid on
  the map comes through them. Nothing here goes near that list.

  ⚠️ It takes no ideo. Section 13 says "none".

  SAFETY
  ======
  The op sits inside a conditional on the def existing, so a missing or
  renamed vessel silences it instead of logging red. Every defName written here
  is vanilla Core, so no `MayRequire` is owed.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Patch>

  <!-- 13 · the Forgotten Arsenal -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="Mechanoid"]</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationSequence">
      <operations>

        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="Mechanoid"]/label</xpath>
          <value><label>the Forgotten Arsenal</label></value>
        </li>

        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="Mechanoid"]/description</xpath>
          <value>
            <description>Not a polity. A standing order that outlived the people who gave it, and the machines that are still carrying it out.\n\nThey wake in buried structures, under drift and under salt, and they resume. Nobody negotiates with the Arsenal because there is nothing there to negotiate with.</description>
          </value>
        </li>

        <!-- The thirteenth bespoke icon (FACTION_ICONS_BESPOKE_1). Mechanoid WRITES
             factionIconPath on the def, so REPLACE matches; an Add would duplicate it.
             CAVEAT, measured 2026-08-21 and not a reason to skip it: this faction is
             hidden=True, settlementGenerationWeight=0 and canMakeRandomly=False, so it
             places no world settlement and the icon has nowhere to draw TODAY. The def
             state is still the correct one, and it costs nothing; if the Forgotten
             Arsenal is ever unhidden or given a holding, its mark is already right. -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="Mechanoid"]/factionIconPath</xpath>
          <value><factionIconPath>World/JawaFactions/ForgottenArsenal</factionIconPath></value>
        </li>

      </operations>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
